  m_Name: _Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: bbec7a84e96ca95458eba143068d1dd0, type: 3}
  title: Rendering Camera Rigs
  sections:
  - heading: Choose a Rig
    text: 'Use one of the listed prefabs to render the desired format. Simply put
      this in place of your scene camera. It is recommended to deactivate any other
      cameras in the scene when rendering. '
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Resolution
    text: Each of the camera rigs renders a specific resolution set in the RenderToDisk
      settings and by the render textures in use. These can be customized as needed.
      It is recommended to duplicate and modify the render textures or create your
      own. For maximum quality, floating point format is recommended.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Render Pipeline
    text: These render setups vary slightly depending on whether you are using URP
      or HDRP. Examples are not provided for the standard pipeline, though they may
      be adapted to it, or any custom render pipeline.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Video Requires FFMPEG
    text: 'In order to use video encoding, FFMPEG will need to be installed on your
      computer and the enviornment path variables setup so that ffmpeg may be executed. '
    linkText: FFMPEG Download & Documentation
    url: https://ffmpeg.org/
  - heading: Relative Output Paths
    text: The wildcards $PROJECT or $ASSETS may be used when setting the output path
      in the RenderToDisk settings to use a path relative to the current project.
      The $PROJECT wildcard is used in each of the examples. If any directories in
      the path do not exist, they will be created automatically.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Additional Comments
    text: Please refer to the comments within each camera rig prefab for additional
      details about each setup.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Rendering Documentation
    text: For further information and a guide to using these rendering features,
      please see the documentation online.
    linkText: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/rendering
    url: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/rendering
  loadedLayout: 0
